package cli

import (
	"context"
	"testing"
	"time"
)

func TestRegressionWorkspaceFamilySurvivesRemovedMember(t *testing.T) {
	env, m := twoRepoWorkspace(t, "gh/acme/a", "release:build", []string{"mise build", "mise deploy"}, "gh/acme/b", "release:ship", []string{"make build", "make release"})
	if _, err := proposeWorkspaceFamilies(context.Background(), env, m, t.TempDir(), "codex", "", "", releaseGroupingAgent(t), time.Now()); err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
	m.Repos = m.Repos[:1]
	if _, err := buildWorkspacePatternCorpus(env, m, time.Now()); err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
	stats, err := proposeWorkspaceFamilies(context.Background(), env, m, t.TempDir(), "codex", "", "", releaseGroupingAgent(t), time.Now())
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
	d, _ := workspaceDir(env, m.Name)
	f := loadAcceptedWorkspaceFamilies(d)
	if len(f) != 0 {
		t.Fatalf("expected reproduction of stale two-member family, got %+v", f)
	}
	t.Logf("current members=%d accepted families=%d verify=%+v", len(m.Repos), len(f), stats)
}

func TestWorkspaceFamilyConsumptionChecksCurrentMembership(t *testing.T) {
	env, m := twoRepoWorkspace(t, "gh/acme/a", "release:build", []string{"mise build", "mise deploy"}, "gh/acme/b", "release:ship", []string{"make build", "make release"})
	if _, err := proposeWorkspaceFamilies(context.Background(), env, m, t.TempDir(), "codex", "", "", releaseGroupingAgent(t), time.Now()); err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
	dir, _ := workspaceDir(env, m.Name)
	families, err := loadAcceptedWorkspaceFamiliesChecked(dir)
	if err != nil || len(families) != 1 {
		t.Fatalf("valid family: %v %v", families, err)
	}
	m.Repos = m.Repos[:1]
	if err := writeWorkspaceManifest(env, m); err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
	families, err = loadAcceptedWorkspaceFamiliesChecked(dir)
	if err != nil || len(families) != 0 {
		t.Fatalf("stale family consumed without refresh: %v %v", families, err)
	}
}
## F41 — P2: substring cues fabricate outcome labels
`reinforcement.go:127–158`: correction/approval cues ignore token boundaries, negation, and whether the next turn is a new task. `TestAuditReinforcementFalseCues` verifies that “Perfect, no need to revert anything.” and “Now add rollback support.” become corrected, while “This is imperfect.” and “I cannot say that it works.” become success. These labels feed both the old episode layer and the corpus outcome path, affecting pattern strengths and generated failure-mode evidence. Use boundary-aware conservative cues and negative/adversarial fixtures; ambiguous utterances should remain neutral. Graph impact for classifyReinforcement (3 direct, 8 transitive) and both cue predicates retained. Brain `doc:c89ef5a81ee3` and `doc:25efb2fea273` record narrow high-precision intent and spot checks, which do not establish precision for these cases. Evidence audit-reinforcement*.



## F42 — P2: dossier verification survives materially changed evidence
`pattern_deep.go:317–339` hashes episode keys/outcomes, fact identifiers, verification command heads, and rounded strength, omitting Parameters, excerpts, failure/recovery text, variants, title, and other verifier inputs. `pattern_verify.go:203–212` then writes the new export while retaining the old verdict when that incomplete fingerprint matches. `TestAuditDeepVerdictSurvivesChangedEvidence` verifies a deployment invocation changed to `mise deploy --unsafe-no-approval`, yet the next verify performs zero calls and reports both dossiers cached. Shallow dossierFingerprint likewise omits variants and anchor end/path/checkpoint fields. Hash the canonical redacted evidence actually supplied to the verifier, excluding self-referential fingerprint fields. Graph deep fingerprint 1 direct/4 transitive and shallow 1 direct/1 transitive; downstream verification and skill formation matter. Brain `doc:a47205c2295e` explicitly requires invalidation on material evidence changes; `doc:7aa28689611d` identifies the accepted deep dossier as a skill formation gate. Evidence audit-dossierfingerprint* and audit-deepfingerprint*.

### Additional comment and test-quality examples
- `reinforcement.go` describes `AgentErrored` as a real-pipeline field, but reinforcementSignal has no such field; the file header says that signal is deferred. correctionPrefixes repeats “no the”.
- `episodes_test.go:249–260` promises a repeated-identical-request collision test, but its fixture contains three different requests.
- `pattern_deep.go` repeats the bounded/deep/full distinction in several nearby comment blocks; consolidate the contract and actual caps. Its three sampled shallow anchors are correct for insertPatternEvidence despite the higher dossier cap.
- `practiceSupportSaturat` and `procedureSupportSaturat` truncate an ordinary word without a useful naming convention.
- `loadBrainEpisodes` swallows every read error. Graph currently identifies only a test caller; do not present this as an active production failure.



## F43 — P2: unchanged transcripts retain obsolete fact corroboration
`pattern_corpus.go:550–553` skips the entire per-session index using only transcript size/mtime/digest/parser version. Fact links are created only inside indexSessionIntoCorpus, although factsByBranch is loaded anew each build. `TestAuditPatternFactLinksStayStale` builds one fact link, retracts the fact, refreshes the corpus, and observes that link still present. Newly distilled facts likewise cannot link to already indexed episodes until the transcript/parser changes. Candidate promotion and dossier evidence therefore keep obsolete corroboration. Rebuild fact enrichment independently or include its relevant input generation in invalidation. Session metadata changes also are absent from this check (source-only observation). Graph corpusSessionUnchanged 1 direct/1 transitive, within buildPatternCorpusLocked. Brain `doc:fc89028aec17` records incremental transcript skipping; it does not justify stale enrichment. Evidence audit-corpusfresh*.



## F44 — P2: skill formation accepts stale verified dossiers
`pattern_skill_deep.go:42–61`: loadAcceptedDeepDossierChecked selects only the saved verdict and payload, ignoring status and current evidence fingerprint. The form path uses it as the acceptance gate (`skill_cmd.go:203,227`). `TestAuditStaleDeepDossierAccepted` sets an accepted dossier to status=stale and confirms it still loads as eligible evidence. This is separate from F42: even a correctly invalidated cache is not rejected at consumption. Require a current verdict bound to the current evidence before claiming VERIFIED to synthesis. Graph: 2 direct/7 transitive callers, including runPatternsSkillsForm. Brain evidence for F42 describes this as the verification gate. Evidence audit-pattern-evidence*, audit-deepaccepted*.



## F45 — P2: the last episode loses its assistant evidence range
`pattern_corpus.go:1265–1269`: endLine starts at startLine and advances only when a following user request exists. The final episode therefore cites only its opening user line regardless of subsequent tool/assistant work. Downstream deep dossiers and theme sampling use that end line to bound excerpts. `TestAuditFinalEpisodeLosesEvidenceRange` builds a three-line user/assistant/assistant transcript and verifies range 1–1. Set the final range to the actual transcript end using dialect-aware source anchors. Graph indexSessionIntoCorpus: 1 direct/1 transitive through corpus build. Brain docs describe exact source spans but no intentional exclusion of final assistant work. Evidence audit-pattern-evidence*, audit-episoderange*.

### Additional test/comment quality findings from patterns
- `pattern_corpus_enrich_test.go:26–33` checks the wrong tool count (4 instead of 2), then only logs: any count passes.
- `pattern_skill_deep_test.go:108–124` claims a golden test proves generic-skill rejection, but the stub unconditionally returns NOT_A_SKILL. It proves response parsing/propagation, not model judgment. The “form requires” test directly calls loaders and synthesis rather than invoking form.
- `pattern_themes.go:15–19` says a deterministic builder proposes themes during refresh; verifyThemes and its tests show proposals are agent-only explicit maintenance.
- `pattern_surface.go` header and loadCorpusDossiersChecked comment still promise graceful unreadable-state handling; checked implementations now return those errors.
- `skill_form.go:102–113` spends a full historical paragraph explaining an environment-variable lookup. Preserve the configured-home contract and move repair history out of the code.



## F46 — P2: skill overwrite modifies outside hard-link targets
`skill_form.go:215`: writeSkillFile checks symlinks but uses os.WriteFile on an existing regular leaf. A hard-linked destination passes these checks and overwrites every alias, including an outside file. `TestAuditSkillHardlinkOverwrite` creates only temporary files and verifies an outside sentinel changes to the skill payload. The CLI normally requires --force for the pre-existing leaf; that authorizes replacement of the named skill, not unrelated aliases. Use an atomic replacement of a newly created regular file (and enforce directory identity at the write boundary). Graph 4 direct/9 transitive callers including repo/workspace synthesizeAndForm. Brain `doc:2a8452b0dc7f` describes containment and hard-link defense elsewhere; no reason found for weaker skill-write semantics. Evidence audit-skillhardlink*.



## F47 — P2: failed validation is presented as recovery
`pattern_deep.go` deepFailureModes uses the first validation command as recovery without checking success or ordering. TestAuditFailedCommandInventsRecovery supplies a single failed `go test`; the dossier claims both “failed: go test” and “re-ran go test to verify”, although no rerun occurred. Require a subsequent successful validation before asserting recovery; otherwise leave it unknown. Graph identifies 1 direct/4 transitive callers. Brain doc:7aa28689611d and doc:8699dd07f315 describe source-grounded correction/recovery evidence. Reproduction and Graph/Brain results: audit-recovery* in evidence.



## F48 — P2: removed workspace members remain in accepted skill families
`pattern_workspace_semantic.go:133–135` returns before invalidating existing families when fewer than two members contribute. Workspace corpus refresh explicitly preserves family dossiers. TestAuditWorkspaceFamilySurvivesRemovedMember creates an accepted two-repo family, removes one member, refreshes and verifies, and still reads the accepted two-repo family. Verification reports all-zero stats without withdrawing it. Clear or invalidate families on loss of eligibility, and validate current membership when consuming them. Graph proposeWorkspaceFamiliesInDB: 1 direct/7 transitive callers including runWorkspacePatternsVerify. Brain doc:7aa28689611d describes cross-repo eligibility and member-evidence fingerprint caching. Evidence audit-family*.

### Further misleading maintenance comments
`patterns_cmd.go:14–19` still describes Phase 1 status-only behavior and a future listing, although the command already lists patterns. `workspace_patterns.go` header describes the legacy JSON implementation, while the primary listing now uses the V2 corpus. Tests using releaseGroupingAgent prove wiring and imposed stub decisions, not semantic grouping or rejection quality.

